    "created_at": "2023-03-06T13:47:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-06T13:47:12Z",
    "body": "Reading the RFC it also suggests that \r\n\r\n* `new URL(\"b\", \"test:a\")` should yield \"`test:b`\", whereas we yield an error https://jsdom.github.io/whatwg-url/#url=Yg==&base=dGVzdDph\r\n* `new URL(\"b\", \"test:c/a\")` should yield \"`test:c/b`\", whereas we yield an error https://jsdom.github.io/whatwg-url/#url=Yg==&base=dGVzdDpjL2E=\r\n\r\nso from that perspective I think we should probably not do this. Being consistent on path and query makes a lot of sense to me.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
