    "created_at": "2023-03-06T21:11:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-06T21:11:13Z",
    "body": "In practice though in opaque path URLs the query is treated as an extension of the path data and not as its own independent thing. And that's also the case in non-opaque path URLs. The path and query together determine what you get back from the server. It's only the fragment that's special and does something locally.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
